  "body": "Stacked on #4207 (branch `issue/1120-verdict-inks`), which is stacked on #4073. Its own commit is c859c79eb. Review that commit only. Merge the PRs under it first.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe last family of #1120: the window chrome inks. After this PR, each colour literal at a draw site in `crates/ui/src` reads a token, and the colour-literal guard has only permanent rows.\n\n- Two colour tokens join `Tokens`. Each is also a theme-file key (`colors.<name>`):\n  - `close_hover`: the hover fill of a floating window's close button (the desktop caption red `#C42B1C`);\n  - `close_ink`: the white cross on it.\n- Both built-in columns hold the old values, so no pixel changes. `window_chrome::CLOSE_HOVER` is gone; `caption` reads the tokens.\n- The `error_text.rs` row of the guard was not a draw site. Its one literal (`Color32::RED`) was in the file's inline test module. Each caller passes a theme or palette ink. The test module moves to `error_text_tests.rs` with no change, and the guard skips it as a test file.\n- The guard rows are now all `keep:` rows: the two token tables (`theme/tables.rs`, 122; `theme/verdict.rs`, 15), the contrast maths and a colour that only measures text. The header says that a new row needs a reason that is not a theme choice.\n- The colour vocabulary has 61 keys. A new test pins it inside the 64-entry map cap of a theme file, as one already pins the geometry vocabulary.\n- The example theme and the colour table of the user guide have the two keys.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1120-chrome-inks.md`.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nAbout 19 viewport line colours are plain-number `[f32; 3]` constants (the move kinds, the region and retract lines, the grid and pick colours in `interact.rs`, the sketch, envelope and boundary hover lines, and their light-ground sets in `ground_ink.rs`). The guard cannot see them, and most of them go to the shaders. They are a separate design (shader inputs and the ground rule). #4209 tracks them.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nIn `crates/ui/tests/theme_files/chrome_inks.rs`, a new module of the existing `theme_files` test binary (#3187: no new binary):\n\n- `the_built_in_columns_keep_the_close_button_colours`: both columns carry the old red and white.\n- `each_close_button_ink_is_a_theme_key`: each key sets its own ink, and the arrow's hover is unchanged.\n- `the_colour_vocabulary_fits_the_map_cap`.\n\nAlso: `colour_literals::no_colour_literal_outside_the_allowed_rows`, `theme_example::example_loads_and_holds_the_dark_defaults`, and the moved `error_text` tests (lib).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe Report an issue window with the pointer on its close button, cropped to the window. Same renderer as #4207. A pixel comparison of the full frame gives 0 different pixels. Before is 25b220b34 (the #4073 head); after is c859c79eb.\n\n| Before (25b220b34) | After (c859c79eb) |\n|---|---|\n| ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-chrome/before-close-hover.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-chrome/after-close-hover.png) |\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the same tree as c859c79eb (the commit message changed from `Refs` to `Fixes` after the gate):\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (2.9 min).\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI. The tests and the pixel comparison pin the values.\n\nChangelog: Themes can set the colours of a floating window's close button (`close_hover`, `close_ink`).\n\nFixes #1120\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
